{
  "description": "Frame-sequence gap detection on private channels in the plain WebSocket client (no helper), with the client option reorder_window_ms from the case. Same step kinds as private_signout.json plus {\"advance_ms\": n}: advance the client's test clock by n ms and run every timer that falls due (the reorder window); SDKs inject this clock for tests, so no case depends on real time. Tracked events: sequence_gap {channel, expected, received} and resync {reason: \"sequence_gap\"} (both once per gap). The first frame after subscribed is the baseline; a number lower than expected is late or duplicate (never a gap); a higher number is a gap only if the missing numbers have not all arrived within reorder_window_ms; after a gap the next expected number is received + 1. Frames without a sequence are ignored.",
